From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: playportdev <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:34:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 240/242] ntdll: limit the [thr-prio] lines per process, not
 per app

madeira-unix 0078 logs each SetThreadPriority and base-priority request
as [thr-prio], up to 200 lines. The limit is a static in the one ntdll
every Wine process of the app shares, and in every RDR2 run the launcher
and its CEF helpers used all 200 before the game started, so what RAGE
asks for its threads was never seen (PLA-364).

The limit is now 200 lines for each of the first 64 Windows processes:
a process claims a slot by its pid with compare-and-swap from 0, and with
the table full nothing more is logged. Each line names the calling
process (pid=). What is set is unchanged; a release build logs none of
it (WINEDEBUG=-all).

Linear: PLA-364
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-30-rdr2-kk-audio-diagnostics.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c
index 7180991..556acdd 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c
@@ -3062,16 +3062,33 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtQueryInformationThread( HANDLE handle, THREADINFOCLASS class,
  * applies none on iOS; log the first 200 requests (the caller's TID, the
  * target's, the class and value) so a title's priorities can be read beside
  * the [xp-qos] census. Measurement only. */
+/* Playport (PLA-364): the 200-line limit is per Windows process, for the
+ * first 64 processes, not for the whole app: the launcher and its CEF helpers
+ * used all 200 before a game started. A process claims a slot by
+ * compare-and-swap from 0; with the table full nothing more is logged. */
+#define IOS_THR_PRIO_PROCESSES 64
+#define IOS_THR_PRIO_LINES 200
 static void ios_log_thread_priority( HANDLE handle, const char *what, LONG value, unsigned int status )
 {
-    static LONG logged;
+    static struct { ULONG pid; LONG logged; } procs[IOS_THR_PRIO_PROCESSES];
     THREAD_BASIC_INFORMATION tbi;
-    ULONG target = 0;
-    if (__atomic_add_fetch( &logged, 1, __ATOMIC_RELAXED ) > 200) return;
+    ULONG target = 0, pid = HandleToULong( NtCurrentTeb()->ClientId.UniqueProcess );
+    int i;
+    for (i = 0; i < IOS_THR_PRIO_PROCESSES; i++)
+    {
+        ULONG seen = __atomic_load_n( &procs[i].pid, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE ), expected = 0;
+        if (seen == pid) break;
+        if (!seen && (__atomic_compare_exchange_n( &procs[i].pid, &expected, pid, FALSE,
+                                                   __ATOMIC_ACQ_REL, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE ) || expected == pid))
+            break;
+    }
+    if (i == IOS_THR_PRIO_PROCESSES) return;
+    if (__atomic_add_fetch( &procs[i].logged, 1, __ATOMIC_RELAXED ) > IOS_THR_PRIO_LINES) return;
     if (!NtQueryInformationThread( handle, ThreadBasicInformation, &tbi, sizeof(tbi), NULL ))
         target = HandleToULong( tbi.ClientId.UniqueThread );
-    ERR( "[thr-prio] tid=%04x target=%04x %s=%d status=%x\n",
-         (unsigned)(ULONG_PTR)NtCurrentTeb()->ClientId.UniqueThread, (unsigned)target, what, (int)value, status );
+    ERR( "[thr-prio] tid=%04x target=%04x %s=%d status=%x pid=%04x\n",
+         (unsigned)(ULONG_PTR)NtCurrentTeb()->ClientId.UniqueThread, (unsigned)target, what, (int)value, status,
+         (unsigned)pid );
 }
 
 /******************************************************************************
